; Run a cutscene until an actor says it is over
;
; Clears the flag #R$8501, sets the room state to $80 (the frame routine runs the game logic, so the actors queued by
; #R$8870 are spawned by #R$8905 and move) and runs the foreground half of the game frame, as the intro does: wait for a
; completed frame list (#R$8869), run it (#R$BDDA), build and copy the cells (#R$97B7, #R$95FF). It stops when an
; actor sets #R$8501 (the end of its path script, #R$B1CF, or its countdown, #R$B97D) and then sets the room state to 0.
; Jean is not in play (state 0) and the keys do nothing.
; .
; Hardware: none directly.
@label=RunCutscene
c$88DE XOR A                ; CutsceneDone = 0
 $88DF LD ($8501),A
@isub=LD A,STATE_RUNNING
 $88E2 LD A,$80
 $88E4 LD ($850C),A         ; RoomState
@label=RunCutscene_Loop
*$88E7 CALL $8869           ; wait for a completed frame list
 $88EA CALL $BDDA           ; = #R$BDDB, run the frame list
 $88ED CALL $97B7
 $88F0 CALL $95FF
 $88F3 LD A,($8501)         ; CutsceneDone
 $88F6 OR A
 $88F7 JR Z,$88E7
 $88F9 XOR A                ; room state 0
 $88FA LD ($850C),A
 $88FD RET
